# Variables: environment, in-place, dynamic, global and request variables.
# Hover over a {{variable}} to see its value and where it comes from.

# In-place variables apply to the whole file
@resource = anything
@url = {{baseUrl}}/{{resource}}

### Environment and in-place variables
GET {{url}}/items?user={{user}}&size={{pageSize}}

### Dynamic variables – a new value for every occurrence
POST {{baseUrl}}/anything
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{$uuid}}",
  "timestamp": {{$timestamp}},
  "iso": "{{$isoTimestamp}}",
  "int": {{$randomInt}},
  "range": {{$random.integer(100, 200)}},
  "float": {{$random.float(0, 1)}},
  "letters": "{{$random.alphabetic(8)}}",
  "code": "{{$random.alphanumeric(12)}}",
  "hex": "{{$random.hexadecimal(16)}}",
  "email": "{{$random.email}}",
  "osUser": "{{$env.USER}}",
  "projectRoot": "{{$projectRoot}}"
}

### Global variables – set by a response handler, used by later requests
# @name createItem
POST {{baseUrl}}/anything
Content-Type: application/json

{"itemId": "{{$random.alphanumeric(6)}}"}

> {%
  client.global.set("itemId", response.body.json.itemId);
  client.log("Stored itemId =", client.global.get("itemId"));
%}

### Uses the global variable from the request above
GET {{baseUrl}}/anything/items/{{itemId}}

### Request variables – set by a pre-request script, only for this request
< {%
  request.variables.set("requestId", $uuid);
  request.variables.set("filter", JSON.stringify({ active: true }));
%}
GET {{baseUrl}}/anything?filter={{filter}}
X-Request-Id: {{requestId}}

### Unresolved variable – the response tab warns about it
GET {{baseUrl}}/anything/{{doesNotExist}}
